Remove 7 and 56 from a string and print a final value.
TCS Digital (27th Jan 2021)

Input - I am Ja7ye56sh Co7d56er
Output - I am Jayesh Coder

Solution - 

import java.util.*;
public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
	Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
	String str = sc.nextLine();
	str=str.replace("56","");
	str=str.replace("7","");
	System.out.println(str);
	}
}
